 - Fixed and enhanced the issue of AI overbuilding defenders in the early game. It now tries (at least in theory in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` anyways etc) to replace the unit to build with an offense of versatile leaning. Typically, this means less longbowmen and more spearmen, camel archers, axemen, etc. We avoid to produce excess siege (in particular trebuchets-like units anyways etc) since they are not versatile enough to be used at defense and offense especially by the AI but anyways etc. The focus and assumption is we'll do good enough early where power differences are still not that great and gains potentially important to make. We also as of now favour civ-specific units (e.g. an egyptian war chariot rather than a horse archer if i'm not mistaken anyways etc) most times. If no good unit candidate is found, we attempt to hijack the unitai of the defensive unit (e.g. a longbowman with attack or attack_city or counter instead of city_defense). Results are very impressive!! They don't seem to always apply or entirely apply, but it does seem like most rivals have significantly less longbowmen and a more varied composition, and sometimes the difference is massive. For example in a run, hatshepsut ai went from +/- 30+ longbowmen for +/- 6 cities at turn 130 to 32 war chariots (plus camel archers for some reason etc), while some ais had often few, sometimes many longbowmen for some reason. Still, overall the seemingly more versatile compositions for all AI players, hopefully helps them better transition into an offensive middle game strategy and not be stuck with useless excess defenders. This should help boxed in players in particular, but also any AI with excess unit, after quite minimal defense needs are met (offense units can defend then as well and are more versatile if i am not mistaken but anyways etc, the varied composition also indirectly helps counter picks to invade us (like building spearmen vs chariots, or axes vs swords, hopefully, but anyways etc)). See originally changes in [53.2 - (Fixed and enhanced) Joao AI building way too many defenders (36 longbowmen at turn 130!! Almost all with UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE or similar) while being boxed in with only 3 cities, instead of making about half of these offense units or versatile ones to punish overextending thin neighbour, fixed by having an early phase "we have expectedly too few cities at this stage of the game, no need to overbuild anymore denders at this stage of the game, switch to offense or versatile UNITAI rather" and "our military composition has way too many defender UNITAIs, switch to offense or versatile UNITAIs", which seemingly fix the issue anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue-anyways-etc) and then a more refined and enhanced, as of now final version of these in [53.2.2 (Seemingly greatly enhanced) AI overproducing defenders early on, especially longbowmen but not only, replaced with an early produce more versatile units especially civ-specific ones when defended enough (at least in theory anyways etc) in CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-anyways-etc-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-anyways-etc) anyways etc.
 - Tremendously improved AI overbuilding trebuchets in particular but more generally siege units, especially when it is bad like being weaker (trebuchets are useless and very hammer inefficient if not strictly to attack city tiles, catapults or cannons or such are also not too versatile or/and used correctly by AI to defend for example). Used various conditions in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to try to make siege units production as minimal as possible, up to none at all if needed, but if other conditions are met but anyways etc hopefully not too low (a bit low as of now but much better than before when it was too strong). As a result, AIs should have a more varied offensive stack composition, as well as being better at defense when weaker, as seems the case in autoplay test i ran at a glance but anyways etc. See for details [53.3 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding siege units, in particular trebuchets but not only, where they are detrimental to do build, in particular when weaker but not only anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc). Update: since then, heavily relaxed renaissance+ siege thresholds in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` and in the fallback unit if no production code as well in `CvCity::doTurn`, as cannons as a viable alternative to a defender, especially if we have no bonus and no access to muskets yet, overbuilding pikemen against cuirassiers is useless, ineffective, and will bankrupt us sooner. Also allows for more varied stacks compositions and much better results ingame for some AIs it seems that had the issue of dying due to having too much pikemen and keeping to build them when cannons are available and much stronger, but check to be sure anyways etc.
 - removed `UNITAI_CITY_COUNTER` from non-versatile enough units such as the UNIT_MACEMAN, as they are not versatile enough to be reliable city defenders while still being good offense units (too easy to punish with a stack of knight units that are good against them, even a crossbow stack could defeat defending macemen, so use them for offense rather and disable them from here as well as in similar places anyways etc). They may be good against pikemen, but pikemen don't often attack cities and are not that efficient for that, so prefer macemen to focus more on offense unitai roles if i am not mistaken but anyways etc, and same for other units if any have that issue as well anyways etc.
-- removed `UNITAI_COUNTER` from mounted units that had it (UNIT_CHARIOT, UNIT_EGYPT_WARCHARIOT, UNIT_CARTHAGE_NUMIDIAN_CAVALRY) as they are not strong enough defender units to warrant it (doesn't ""receive defense bonuses" (i.e. modifiers if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc), plus takes a longbowman slot inefficiently as well i mean if i may say but anyways etc), and are wasted as a non attacker (stays parked in cities sometimes for example for the egyptian war chariot if i remember it correctly anyways etc) if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc. For chariot class units in particular, it may have made sense when longbows were available much later, but now in our mod but anyways etc they are available at about same time in tech as axeman class units but anyways etc, and are a more versatile, cheap enough and overall stronger defender, so prefer it for that purpose rather and use chariots offensively if in window to do so else don't build them (rather than park them in cities if i am not mistaken but anyways etc).
+- removed `UNITAI_COUNTER` from mounted units that had it (UNIT_CHARIOT, UNIT_EGYPTIAN_WAR_CHARIOT, UNIT_CARTHAGE_NUMIDIAN_CAVALRY) as they are not strong enough defender units to warrant it (doesn't ""receive defense bonuses" (i.e. modifiers if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc), plus takes a longbowman slot inefficiently as well i mean if i may say but anyways etc), and are wasted as a non attacker (stays parked in cities sometimes for example for the egyptian war chariot if i remember it correctly anyways etc) if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc. For chariot class units in particular, it may have made sense when longbows were available much later, but now in our mod but anyways etc they are available at about same time in tech as axeman class units but anyways etc, and are a more versatile, cheap enough and overall stronger defender, so prefer it for that purpose rather and use chariots offensively if in window to do so else don't build them (rather than park them in cities if i am not mistaken but anyways etc).
 - Tremendously improved AI overbuilding very cheap (as of now 20 or less hammer cost in unitinfo XML (indepent from any trainpercent modifier if i am not mistaken anyways etc)) combat units (ancient macemen only being an issue as of now anyways etc) in the early game, sometimes even at turn 100, which is inefficient, nonsensical since there are so many better options like swordsmen, chariots, longbowmen, anything else basically some of which not requiring any bonus if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc, and easy to overshoot if i may say but anyways etc, as they are cheap and accumulate quickly, but are not too effective especially as soon as we get archer units anyways etc, now limited, especially even more so after as of now turn 50 where they should be especially useless. Since they are easy to overbuild due to being so cheap, they may quickly make us bankrupt, and are not so effective per unit. As in our mod archers are as of now available very soon, fairly cheap, and more versatile and overall stronger, plus since they also help fill our defense needs/quotas sooner so we move to offense focus sooner, it seems very nice to be able to cut down on excess very cheap units, as of now only the ancient maceman (note: this trims down scouts as well since they have combat if i am not mistaken, but we don't seem to overproduce them so fine anyways etc, and even if we were to then would be handled by the same cap if i am not mistaken but anyways etc). As a result of these changes in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, ingame, we seem to have much better compositions (e.g. 3 ancient macemen at turn 100-130 vs 11 before in AI players), and much more stronger units in comparison. Hopefully helps being economically efficient as well. AI should be stronger as a result of these changes hopefully if i am not mistaken but anyways etc. See for details [53.4 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding very cheap combat units (ancient macemen only being an issue as of now anyways etc) in the early game, sometimes even at turn 100, which is inefficient and easy to overshoot if i may say but anyways etc, as they are cheap and accumulate quickly, but are not too effective especially as soon as we get archer units anyways etc, now limited, especially even more so after as of now turn 50 where they should be especially useless; much better military compositions and better growth as a result anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#534-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-very-cheap-combat-units-ancient-macemen-only-being-an-issue-as-of-now-anyways-etc-in-the-early-game-sometimes-even-at-turn-100-which-is-inefficient-and-easy-to-overshoot-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-as-they-are-cheap-and-accumulate-quickly-but-are-not-too-effective-especially-as-soon-as-we-get-archer-units-anyways-etc-now-limited-especially-even-more-so-after-as-of-now-turn-50-where-they-should-be-especially-useless-much-better-military-compositions-and-better-growth-as-a-result-anyways-etc) anyways etc. Update: now the anti excess very cheap units is also included in `CvCity::doTurn` in the no production fallback unit code, as we were producing too many fallback ancient macemen otherwise with the new offense only code (like 19 ancient macemen at turn 100 which is very inefficient and most likely to bankrupt us or ruin our game but anyways etc) anyways etc.
 
