 - **Very cheap-combat spam cap (tiered & generalized):** The AI was **overbuilding very cheap combat units**—notably the **Ancient Maceman**—even ~T100. Because they’re so cheap, they pile up, are weak once Archers appear, and can drag the economy. We added conditions in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to **limit** these builds, with a **stricter cap after ~T50** when they’re especially poor value. In SAS, Archers arrive early, are cheap/versatile, and fill defense quotas sooner, letting cities pivot to offense. (Scouts get trimmed incidentally since they’re combat-tagged, though they weren’t the main issue.) **Result:** more varied, stronger stacks (e.g., ~3 Ancient Macemen @T100–130 vs ~11 before) and a **healthier economy**. See [KI#53.4](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#534-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-very-cheap-combat-units-ancient-macemen-only-being-an-issue-as-of-now-anyways-etc-in-the-early-game-sometimes-even-at-turn-100-which-is-inefficient-and-easy-to-overshoot-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-as-they-are-cheap-and-accumulate-quickly-but-are-not-too-effective-especially-as-soon-as-we-get-archer-units-anyways-etc-now-limited-especially-even-more-so-after-as-of-now-turn-50-where-they-should-be-especially-useless-much-better-military-compositions-and-better-growth-as-a-result-anyways-etc). **Update:** The cap is now **generalized beyond Ancient** using **tier-based (not era-based) thresholds** to avoid era bleed-through (e.g., Ancient Macemen don’t inherit looser Classical caps). This also aims to trim (at least in theory, data lacking to draw a conclusion on an experiment anyways etc) for example **Archers in Classical** and **Longbows/Triremes in Medieval** when they’re too cheap for their tier. In practice we see AI mixes improve (e.g., Japan AI shifting from ~75 Longbows @T200 to ~50–60 Longbows + 10–15 Camel Archers + 20–27 Samurai, run-dependent). Tunables live in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` and [`GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml`](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml). **Update (fallback production):** Applied the same cap inside CvCity::doTurn’s **no-production fallback** so that the **new offense-only** alternative logic no longer spams **Ancient Macemen** (e.g., ~19 @T100).
 
